{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JVXrn4ADZB63ePyRE47a3S","type":"tool_result","content":"argocd-overview-2026-08-23.md:11:Argo CD is a declarative, GitOps continuous delivery tool for Kubernetes.\nargocd-overview-2026-08-23.md:20:[Omitted long matching line]\ncncf-landscape-and-community-2026-08-23.md:11:[Omitted long matching line]\nflux-concepts-2026-08-23.md:10:Flux is a GitOps Toolkit: a set of composable APIs and specialized tools that can be used to build Continuous Delivery on top of Kubernetes. GitOps is a way of managing your infrastructure and applications so that whole system is described declaratively and version controlled, and having an automated process that ensures that the deployed environment matches the state specified in one or more Git repositories.\nk8s-docs-overview-2026-08-23.md:29:- **Self-healing** — Kubernetes restarts containers that fail, replaces containers, kills containers that don't respond to your user-defined health check, and doesn't advertise them to clients until they are ready to serve.\nk8s-docs-overview-2026-08-23.md:41:- Does not deploy source code and does not build your application. Continuous Integration, Delivery, and Deployment (CI/CD) workflows are determined by organization cultures and preferences as well as technical requirements.\nk8s-docs-overview-2026-08-23.md:45:- Does not provide nor adopt any comprehensive machine configuration, maintenance, management, or self-healing systems.\nk8s-docs-service-accounts-2026-08-23.md:16:Your Pods need to communicate with the Kubernetes API server (reading Secrets, cross-namespace access); your Pods need to communicate with an external service that requires an identity; authenticating to a private image registry using an imagePullSecret; an external service needs to communicate with the Kubernetes API server (CI/CD pipelines); you use third-party security software that relies on the ServiceAccount identity of different Pods to group those Pods into different contexts.\nk8s-docs-topology-spread-constraints-2026-08-24.md:58:> self-heal in the case that there is a problem."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1c450c9f-3efb-4615-9d77-0943167fd975","uuid":"bf9f6dd1-f6b3-41f4-8ee9-95968444b31d","timestamp":"2026-08-31T09:56:36.596Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"argocd-overview-2026-08-23.md:11:Argo CD is a declarative, GitOps continuous delivery tool for Kubernetes.\nargocd-overview-2026-08-23.md:20:[Omitted long matching line]\ncncf-landscape-and-community-2026-08-23.md:11:[Omitted long matching line]\nflux-concepts-2026-08-23.md:10:Flux is a GitOps Toolkit: a set of composable APIs and specialized tools that can be used to build Continuous Delivery on top of Kubernetes. GitOps is a way of managing your infrastructure and applications so that whole system is described declaratively and version controlled, and having an automated process that ensures that the deployed environment matches the state specified in one or more Git repositories.\nk8s-docs-overview-2026-08-23.md:29:- **Self-healing** — Kubernetes restarts containers that fail, replaces containers, kills containers that don't respond to your user-defined health check, and doesn't advertise them to clients until they are ready to serve.\nk8s-docs-overview-2026-08-23.md:41:- Does not deploy source code and does not build your application. Continuous Integration, Delivery, and Deployment (CI/CD) workflows are determined by organization cultures and preferences as well as technical requirements.\nk8s-docs-overview-2026-08-23.md:45:- Does not provide nor adopt any comprehensive machine configuration, maintenance, management, or self-healing systems.\nk8s-docs-service-accounts-2026-08-23.md:16:Your Pods need to communicate with the Kubernetes API server (reading Secrets, cross-namespace access); your Pods need to communicate with an external service that requires an identity; authenticating to a private image registry using an imagePullSecret; an external service needs to communicate with the Kubernetes API server (CI/CD pipelines); you use third-party security software that relies on the ServiceAccount identity of different Pods to group those Pods into different contexts.\nk8s-docs-topology-spread-constraints-2026-08-24.md:58:> self-heal in the case that there is a problem.","numLines":9,"totalLines":9}}
